From: hIRoic Linux hammer PoC <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: mmci: add opt-in single-block request limit

The STM32F746 SDMMC external-DMA path leaves data in the MMCI FIFO for
larger block-layer requests, after which MMCI disables DMA and falls back to
the non-working PIO transmit path.  Allow the board DT to bound requests to
one 512-byte sector, matching the established Zephyr hammer configuration
for this hardware.

Upstream-status: Inappropriate [board-specific stability quirk]
---
 drivers/mmc/host/mmci.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.c b/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.c
@@ -2200,6 +2200,15 @@ static int mmci_probe(struct amba_device *dev,
 	 */
 	mmc->max_blk_count = mmc->max_req_size >> variant->datactrl_blocksz;
 
+	if (np && of_property_read_bool(np, "st,force-single-block")) {
+		mmc->max_segs = 1;
+		mmc->max_req_size = 512;
+		mmc->max_seg_size = 512;
+		mmc->max_blk_count = 1;
+		dev_info(&dev->dev,
+			 "limiting transfers to one 512-byte block\n");
+	}
+
 	spin_lock_init(&host->lock);
 
 	writel(0, host->base + MMCIMASK0);
-- 
2.51.0
